deferred_proposals.detail:
Build from full_results.pkl all_trades (430 round trips including the reference sleeves).

(a) Strip plot: trade P&L against entry date per sleeve (S1C, S3, S4 solid; S1/S2 reference faint). Colour by sign, size by holding days. Mark the open trade.

(b) Histograms of holding days and per-trade P&L.

(c) Per-sleeve table:
- closed n, P(profit);
- mean and median trade;
- best and worst trade;
- share of sleeve P&L from the 5 largest trades;
- median holding days.

(d) Worst-drawdown table, top 5 per series: peak, valley, recovery date or 'not recovered', depth, duration. The portfolio itself is 'not recovered' since its first peak.

Set and enforce one house style:
- vol levels in % (σ = 19.45%);
- vol differences and errors in 'vol pts' (never 'vp');
- VIX-family levels in index pts (no '%': today the Overview shows 'VIX 19.45 %' while axes say 'vol pts' and Model Risk says 'index pts');
- half-spreads 'hs' defined once;
- $ with k/M suffixes;
- signs as model - market and implied - realised, stated in each table caption.

Add a 'Definitions' section, reachable from the existing '?' overlay and a footer link: one anchor per term, each with formula, units and where it is used. The first occurrence of each term per page becomes <dfn>/<abbr title> linking to it.

At ≤ 600 px:
- status strip becomes one line: 'STALE · fit 5 sessions ▸', where ▸ is a <details> showing all source dates (no JS needed);
- ticker becomes 2 rows (SPX, VIX, VVIX / slope, ratio, rule);
- stale banner becomes one line with the cause from Q3b and a details disclosure;
- Calibration moves the 3-sentence gate explanation below the parameter tiles.
The staleness signal must stay visible, coloured and textual.
